From 6795a2adb56b84e3958723bf3690fe5d2adc9e28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:15:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 257/406] Make Drawing: a JIS sheet with the views, center
 lines, sizes and title block at once
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"Make Drawing" (tool strip, start page) now goes straight to a finished
first drawing of the picked part (all parts if none is picked): the three
views (front at the largest flat face, standard scale) on an A4 sheet with
a title block (ISO 5457, the default template when the drawing standard is
JIS), placed clear of the title block; a dash-dot cross through each hole;
the holes' size once for holes of the same size ("4×⌀6 キリ"); the overall
width and height of the front view and the depth on the right view; the
title block filled in from the model (name of the file, scale, date, sheet,
general tolerances JIS B 0405-m). The views can still be turned afterwards.
Tested without the GUI: FreeCADCmd -t TestDrawingAuto.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
